abstract: >-
  We present Berna R5, a language model architecture in which knowledge is
  stored in dynamic weighted cells that are born, split, and interconnect
  according to a 6-dimensional knowledge state space. We prove five
  theorems: saturation equilibrium, reliable incorporation, zero-forgetting,
  balanced growth, and plexus connectivity convergence.
keywords:
  - language models
  - continual learning
  - zero-forgetting
  - mixture-of-experts
  - bio-inspired architecture
